# W21: the VM manager. asura-vmd is the engine (a bash script over quickemu and quickget);
# asura-vm is what the keybind, the .desktop file and the QML all call, and it passes engine verbs
# on to asura-vmd. asura-vm-mon is live control of a running guest, asura-vm-ssh the Remotes
# plate's engine. The window's QML (shell/vm.qml, shell/vm/) ships with the shell tree.
# asura-vm-fetch, Ryoku's parallel downloader, is deliberately not built: see docs/vm.md.
asura-vm/mon -> /usr/bin/asura-vm-mon
asura-vm/remote -> /usr/bin/asura-vm-ssh
desktop/cmd/asura-vm/asura-vmd -> /usr/bin/asura-vmd
session/asura-vm -> /usr/bin/asura-vm
session/applications/asura-vm.desktop -> /usr/share/applications/asura-vm.desktop
